{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650961,"nonce":"XGuqqP4UbJSmq9arheQxMU79E4M=","title":"auth-merge leaves protected branch worktree in mid-merge state when YubiKey signing is interrupted","message":"When `auth-merge` runs `git merge --gpg-sign ...` and the YubiKey signing step is interrupted or times out mid-execution, the merge is left in an incomplete state: files are staged and MERGE_HEAD is set, but no merge commit was created. The worktree is now dirty with a partial merge in progress.\n\n**Incident (2026-03-03, feedbax repo):** Auth request for `feature/graph-node-reversal` → `develop` failed with exit_code 1 and output \"Working tree is dirty.\" This was the Mandible executor reporting the state of the worktree after a previous interrupted merge attempt had left staged changes and MERGE_HEAD present.\n\n**Recovery:** User had to manually run `git merge --continue` in the worktree after the signing step completed.\n\n**Fix:** In auth-merge pre-checks, detect the MERGE_HEAD condition (`git rev-parse MERGE_HEAD 2\u003e/dev/null`) and emit a clear \"merge in progress, run `git merge --continue` to finish\" message instead of the generic dirty-worktree error.\n\n**Status:** Fixed in dotfiles retro-fixes branch. This issue tracks the fix landing in the standalone repo.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue cd8c2a5.","files":null}]}